Seeded defect for tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/StoreModelTests.cs

Hand-made: StorageEngine.FreePageOnCommit frees the page at once instead of queueing it until
the transaction commits (the defect of #233, fixed in 4d3e6b9). An update or delete of a
document with overflow pages inside a caller-owned transaction then releases the committed
document's overflow page while the committed document still points at it.

With it applied, 4 of the 8 runs fail on upstream 0450b97 (the single-process ones; in
multi-process mode FreePage queues every page). Each shrinks to 4 steps, e.g. seed 2:
    1. Insert(id=74, count=3, code=c08, payload=18000 chars)
    2. Begin
    3. Update(id=74, count=1, code=c29, payload=0 chars)
    4. Backup
  the backup: document 74: payload differs at index 16187: expected 18000 chars of "l", got "............"

Reproduce: git apply --ignore-whitespace tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/Seeds/StoreModelTests.free-page-before-commit.patch && dotnet test tests/BLite.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~StoreModelTests
Restore:   git checkout -- src

The source file uses CRLF line endings; apply with --ignore-whitespace if the patch was
normalised. Never commit the seeded state.

diff --git a/src/BLite.Core/Storage/StorageEngine.Memory.cs b/src/BLite.Core/Storage/StorageEngine.Memory.cs
index a70bee1..206c661 100644
--- a/src/BLite.Core/Storage/StorageEngine.Memory.cs
+++ b/src/BLite.Core/Storage/StorageEngine.Memory.cs
@@ -178,6 +178,8 @@ public sealed partial class StorageEngine
         if (transactionId == 0)
             throw new InvalidOperationException("Cannot defer a free without a transaction (transactionId=0 is reserved)");
 
+        // SEEDED DEFECT (#233): free the page at once instead of when the transaction commits.
+        if (transactionId != 0) { FreePage(pageId); return; }
         var pages = _freeOnCommit.GetOrAdd(transactionId, _ => new HashSet<uint>());
         lock (pages)
             pages.Add(pageId);
